[Chapter "Giuoco Pianissimo (3...Bc5)"]
[Line "The slow build-up"]
[Opening "Italian Game: Classical Variation, Giuoco Pianissimo"]

{Both sides develop quietly. White's plan is castling, Re1 and a4, keeping d4 in reserve.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Bc5 4. c3 {Prepare d4 for later, and give the bishop a retreat square on b3.} 4... Nf6 5. d3 {The modern, slow approach (Giuoco Pianissimo): keep e4 solid and build up before opening the centre.} 5... d6 6. O-O {Castle.} 6... O-O 7. Re1 {Support e4 and prepare d4 for later.} 7... a6 8. a4 {Gain space on the queenside and stop ...b5, which would chase the c4 bishop.} *
